      "id": "P1-S3",
      "pIndex": 1
    },
    "text": "While polls show Britons rate \"the countryside\" alongside the royal family, Shakespeare and the National Health Service (NHS) as what makes them proudest of their country, this has limited political support.",
    "translation": "尽管民调显示，英国人将“乡村”与王室、莎士比亚以及国家医疗服务体系（NHS）并列为最令他们为国家感到自豪的事物，但在政界这种情结所获得的实质支持却极其有限。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": {
      "structureType": "主从复合句（while引导的让步状语从句 + 宾语从句 + rate A alongside B as C结构 + what引导的宾语从句）",
      "mainClause": "this has limited political support.",
      "modifiers": "While 引导让步状语从句；polls show 后面接省略 that 的宾语从句；Britons 为从句主语，rate 为谓语，the countryside 为直接宾语，alongside the royal family... 为并列介词短语作伴随修饰，as what makes them proudest of their country 为介词短语作宾语补足语，其中 what 引导从句作 as 的宾语。",
      "corePattern": "rate A alongside B as C（将A与B并列评价为C）；make sb. proud of sth.（使某人为某事感到自豪）；limited political support（有限的政治支持）。"
    },
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": true,
      "isKeyEvidence": true
    },
    "provenance": {
